  ordered_supporting_artifacts
  ordered_binding_artifacts
  root_review_required
  provider_calls
  model_calls
  network_calls
  connector_calls
  external_drs_calls
  authority_created
  permission_created
  action_commit_packet_created
  receipt_created
  final_output_created
  drs_write_created
  real_world_effects_count

FractalRuntimeExecutionBundleV02 preserves its former 27-field prefix and adds
only the trailing defaulted observed_work_context field. A baseline context
must contain a publicly valid bundle whose observed_work_context is None.

The baseline anchor is a domain-separated hash of complete canonical public
bundle material excluding the new context field. Public ABI/plain seams and
canonical JSON are used. repr, asdict, id(), and hidden registry values are not
used. Context plain projection replaces the bundle with the anchor and projects
KernelArtifact values through the Kernel ABI plain-data seam.

The binding artifact profile is exact:
  artifact_type=ValidatedEvidence
  schema_version=v0.2
  source_component=fractal_runtime_v02
  authority_class=EVIDENCE_ONLY
  lifecycle_state=VALIDATED
  prefix=frobservedwork_v02:
  domain=HEDGEHOG_FRACTAL_RUNTIME_V02_OBSERVED_WORK_BINDING_ARTIFACT

Its top-level payload keys are exactly change_proof, execution, profile,
safety, source_pair, topology_binding in canonical lexical order. Safety fields
are exact zero/false values. Root parents are topology, baseline source,
observed source. Child parents append the validated activation-parent queue
artifact.

Canonical ordering is rederived from topology-node position, cell depth, cell
ID, baseline source ID, observed source ID, and the canonical changed-pointer
tuple. Direct sources are ordered by binding use; support uses deterministic
parent-before-child Kahn order with lexical artifact-ID tie-break; affected
nodes/cells follow baseline topology/cell order. Caller tuple order cannot
change context or binding identities.

