===============================================================================
6. Transition / t02 / Settled-Prefix Audit
===============================================================================

Transition structural validation recognizes six disjoint parent forms:
  historical root initial: topology artifact
  historical child initial: topology artifact, activation-parent queue artifact
  contextual root initial: topology artifact, ordered binding-artifact suffix
  contextual child initial: topology artifact, activation-parent queue artifact,
    ordered binding-artifact suffix
  successor without result: topology artifact, predecessor queue artifact
  successor with result: topology artifact, predecessor queue artifact,
    result artifact

The initial classifier requires payload state=PENDING, prior_state=None,
predecessor_relation=INITIAL_NONE, and payload parent_cell_id to distinguish
root from child. It does not classify only by len(parent_refs). Structural
positions and prefixes are checked, duplicate and self parents are rejected,
and contextual G2-D validation reconstructs the exact binding objects so a
foreign prefix-valid artifact cannot substitute.

Structural Transition validation remains separate from contextual binding
object validation. No string-only sidecar substitutes for the grouped context.

_d3_validate_settled_runtime_prefix_v02 performs context validation and exact
queue/binding reconstruction. Every internal caller propagates context either
explicitly or through _d4_prefix_kwargs_v02. _d4_run_runtime_v02,
_d4_initialize_runtime_state_v02, _d4_prefix_kwargs_v02, and _d4_indexes_v02
carry the same context object. The three final D3 helper call sites explicitly
pass observed_work_context=None on the historical path.

===============================================================================
7. Stable Cell Witness and Selective Execution Audit
===============================================================================

The root witness independently calls derive_fractal_root_cell_id_v02 with the
baseline source-binding ID, runtime-policy ID, accepted mode, and accepted scope.
It requires equality with both the carried cell ID and topology root cell ID.

The child witness derives canonical_child_index from the validated parent input
and reconstructs the child ID from topology seed, parent cell, child index,
source-binding mode/profile/scope/policy values, exact required downstream
capabilities, runtime forbidden claims, child depth, and the validated scope
projection. projection.child_scope_ref must equal cell_input.scope_ref. The
activation-parent queue artifact is validated and included in child binding
parents. Caller-selected root or child IDs cannot pass.

Topology node membership, assignment identity, cell/node membership, projection
membership, and activation witness remain bound to the immutable baseline.
Route, source binding, topology seed, node, edge, assignment, topology, and
topology artifact identities remain stable.

Selective execution computes direct affected nodes and the minimal applicable
dependency/control closure. Unselected sibling cells retain their existing
cell inputs, queue artifacts, and result artifacts and receive no binding
parents. Baseline objects are not reissued as new outputs. Trace, report, and
report-artifact identities change through validated context lineage.

run_fractal_runtime_v02 is not the normal selective path. It accepts only a
WHOLE_RUN_ESCALATION context at its context seam. A SELECTIVE context fails
closed. Whole-run escalation carries nonempty exact reason/policy identifiers,
uses the same binding/context law, remains Root-review required, and creates no
authority or effects.

===============================================================================
8. Stage-D / Parent-Closed / Pointer Audit
===============================================================================

Observed-work input evidence is a distinct family from historical Stage-D
artifacts. _d4_stage_artifacts_v02 is AST-equivalent to its historical parent
implementation: Stage-D A/B/C queue/result partition semantics and cardinality
remain unchanged. runtime_trace.abi_artifact_refs does not absorb direct source,
support, or binding evidence.

The implementation keeps these logical partitions distinct:
  stage artifacts: proposal, decision, route, topology, queue/result/report
  input evidence: direct source, support-only closure, binding artifacts
  parent-closed union: the canonical union used for contextual validation

The union rejects duplicate-unequal, omitted, foreign, self-parent, cyclic, and
unknown-parent material. Parent-before-child Kahn ordering and lexical
artifact-ID tie-break are deterministic. Kernel ABI bundle and causal-bundle
validators are applied to the resulting closed family.

The RFC-6901 implementation operates over the complete public KernelArtifact
plain mapping. It supports whole artifact pointer "", whole payload
"/payload", payload-relative normalization, deterministic nonempty leaf
expansion, escaped mapping keys, list indexes, and envelope leaves including
time_envelope, trace_refs, parent_refs, source_component, lifecycle_state, and
other accepted fields. Artifact identity and exact predecessor normalization
are treated explicitly. Hard boundary fields such as owner, transaction,
artifact type, schema, ABI, and authority class cannot silently change.
Malformed, incomplete, duplicate, absent, or unrepresentable pointer claims
fail closed. Generated CausalConsumptionRef output pointers are nonempty.

===============================================================================
9. Counterfactual Semantics and Identity Audit
===============================================================================

The historical validate_fractal_runtime_causal_counterfactual_v02 function is
AST-equivalent to the parent implementation and continues to mutate its exact
historical causal source.

The separate observed-work seam accepts only an exact causal row with:
  disposition=USED
  decision_effect=OBSERVED_WORK_INPUT
  reason_code=used:g2d_observed_work_input
  source=the context binding artifact
  downstream=the affected initial queue artifact

Source lookup is from the validated RuntimeObservedWorkContextV02. A mutation
must change exactly the selected represented full-artifact pointer, preserve
hard fields and predecessor law, and rebuild every binding that names the
mutated observed source. It then rebuilds the context and affected execution
lineage.

For USED, the private candidate bundle is completely validated and requires
changes to binding artifact, context, direct initial queue artifact, affected
cell input, affected result artifact, runtime trace, runtime report, and report
artifact. Route, runtime source binding, topology and unaffected closed objects
remain preserved.

For an accepted lifecycle gate stop, the report is PASS with the candidate
disposition BLOCKED_BY_GATE, one nonempty canonical context-derived causal ref,
no candidate bundle identities, and null trace/report/report-artifact IDs.
Malformed, substituted, wrong-pointer, unclosed, authority-changing, or
effect-changing material fails closed.

Successful validated_object_id law:
  prefix=frcounterfactual_v02:
  domain=HEDGEHOG_FRACTAL_RUNTIME_V02_OBSERVED_WORK_COUNTERFACTUAL
  top-level material keys=baseline,candidate,preserved,profile

The exact nested keys are checked in source and tests. The identity material is
canonicalized before hashing and does not contain the returned validated ID;
the counterfactual identity graph is acyclic.

===============================================================================
10. Performance and Cache-Law Audit
===============================================================================

The private _observed_work_bindings_for_cell_node_v02 lookup validates local
type/topology/baseline relations and scans the already validated grouped
binding tuple. It does not call the complete public context validator for each
queue lookup. Public context/plain/source boundaries, settled-prefix entry,
bundle validation, Stage-D validation, causal validation, and whole-run entry
retain validation boundaries.

Success caches are bounded optimization maps keyed by complete recursively
type-tagged structural freezes. They store only prior success and do not use
id(), object identity, authority state, mutable caller-selected keys, or reverse
lookup. They are clearable, bounded, and semantically transparent; they are not
an identity or authority registry. Unsupported, cyclic, or unfreezable values
receive no cache key.

The regression test wraps the public context validator, performs one accepted
private binding lookup, and requires zero repeated public-validator calls in
that lookup. No identity material or execution outcome depends on cache state.

